# The session's brief

What jagt tells a task's session at each step, one `## <step>` section per step. Copy this file to
`session-brief.md` beside `jagt.yml` and edit a section to change what your sessions are told; a section your
copy lacks is read from here, and at a step left empty the session hears jagt's facts alone.

## deploy

Make sure the deploy landed: the pipeline that deploys it passed and the commit above is live on its branch.
If it did, or nothing here can tell, report nothing: end your turn with one line naming what you checked, or
that nothing could. If it did not, report IN_PROGRESS saying what failed, fix it, and hand the round back as
usual — it is reviewed, deployed and checked again.

## verify

jagt ran this project's verification command and it failed with the output above. Fix it, leave the fix
uncommitted, and report REVIEW_PENDING again.

## probes

jagt ran the acceptance probes of the plan you were given a go on, and those above failed. Make them pass, leave
the fix uncommitted, and report REVIEW_PENDING again. A probe that is itself wrong changes only with a new plan:
write it into plan.md and report PLAN_PENDING.

## plan

Start on it.

## round-not-ready

The review of your round came back NOT READY. Each line above is a review comment: fix it, or where you believe
it wrong, change nothing for it and write in task_notes.md `disputed: <the comment> — <evidence>`. A `show:`
comment asks for evidence: answer it the same way. Evidence is a ticket line, a file:line, or a command and what
it printed: the reviewer checks evidence and cannot read your reasons. A line ending [repeat] came back from an
earlier round. Ask (rule 1) only for a decision nobody gave you. Leave the fix uncommitted and report
REVIEW_PENDING again.

## plan-not-ready

The Master read plan.md against the ticket: NOT READY. Rework the plan for each line above. Where you believe one
wrong, change nothing for it and write in task_notes.md `disputed: <the comment> — <evidence>`. Then report
PLAN_PENDING again.

## plan-answered

## asked-human

Your status already carries the question. Report nothing and end your turn; the human answers in this window.
Then report IN_PROGRESS, apply the answer uncommitted, and hand the round back.

## answered

Report IN_PROGRESS, apply it, and hand the round back as usual.

## answered-under

Apply it, then carry on with the instruction above.

## repo

Work there as in your other repositories.

## wake

Continue where you stopped.

## conflict

That worktree is yours until it deploys, and finishing its merge is not a `git merge` of yours. Resolve it there,
never in your own worktree, keeping what both sides meant. Build or test what the project lets you, then
`git add` every resolved path in one go: once nothing is unmerged and nothing is left unstaged, jagt finishes the
deploy. Do not commit, push or report a status. If a side cannot be kept without a human's call, report
outcome=question.
